; Cram tests: each .t file is a transcript of commands and their expected
; output. `dune test` runs them and shows any difference; after an intended
; change, `dune promote` accepts the new output.
;
; Dune reruns a test only when one of these changes, so the SymPy worker is
; listed too: without it, a change there would pass on old output.

(cram
 (deps
  %{bin:landau}
  %{project_root}/cas/worker.py
  (glob_files %{project_root}/modules/*.lan)
  (glob_files_rec cases/**.lan)))
